    {
      "cell": 0,
      "line": 5,
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "The CoT data and part of the hyperparameter settings used in this notebook are adapted from Tong Hui Kang’s open-source GitHub repository, while the training code is modified based on konbu17’s public notebook."
    },
    {
      "cell": 0,
      "line": 6,
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "- [Tong Hui Kang’s open-source GitHub repository](https://github.com/tonghuikang/nemotron)"
    },
    {
      "cell": 0,
      "line": 7,
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "- [konbu17’s public notebook](https://www.kaggle.com/code/konbu17/nemotron-sft-lora-with-cot)"
    },
    {
      "cell": 0,
      "line": 11,
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "In this notebook, I will try to reproduce the method released by Tong Hui Kang and train a model that can reach around **0.85** on the public leaderboard."
    },
    {
      "cell": 0,
      "line": 13,
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "In this version, training on **\"lm_head\"** in target_modules has been **removed**. At the same time, the microbatch size has been reset to **1**. In my experiments, increasing the microbatch size to 2 reduced training time by about **3 h..."
    },
    {
      "cell": 0,
      "line": 15,
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "## Notes on Training"
    },
    {
      "cell": 0,
      "line": 17,
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "Setting per_device_train_batch_size to 2 and gradient_accumulation_steps to 16 can reduce the training time to around **4 hours** while maintaining similar performance **(0.84–0.85)**. However, given the nature of the competition, a scor..."
    },
    {
      "cell": 0,
      "line": 19,
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "It may be possible to restore training performance comparable to that of a microbatch size of 1 through **further hyperparameter tuning**."
    },
    {
      "cell": 2,
      "line": 7,
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "if hasattr(sys.stdout, \"reconfigure\"):"
    },
    {
      "cell": 2,
      "line": 8,
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")"
    },
    {
      "cell": 2,
      "line": 9,
      "kind": "code",
      "text": "if hasattr(sys.stderr, \"reconfigure\"):"
    },
    {
      "cell": 2,
